% M7-T21 / D-0084: A REFUTATION THE CHECKER REJECTED, found by a random sweep of small
% element models (seed 9044). FIXED; an ordinary passing model test whose proof is
% verified on every run.
%
% THE DEFECT. x4 is the INDEX of the second element and the RESULT of the third; x6 the
% other way round. The root conflict in the third excludes a position whose value is an
% interior hole in its result x4, and [excl_hole] cites that hole by its remover's
% explanation -- here the SECOND element's INDEX removal, which (1) concluded in the
% direct currency `~x4_eq_2` where [excl_hole] pairs off ORDER literals, and (2) kept the
% root-established residue `x6_ge_5` its own exclusion carried. The conclusion row was
% `3 ~x4_ge_3 3 x4_ge_2 3 x6_ge_5 3 ~x4_eq_2 >= 4`, and 3.0.2 answered "The constraint
% with ID 121 is not contradicting, as specified by the hint."
%
% THE FIX is in lib/core/prop/element.ml's [filter_index]: an interior index removal's
% explanation cancels its root-established residue and is restated over the order
% encoding through the forward channelling line ([in_order_currency]) -- the form every
% other hole in the store is stated in. No SAT twin: the defect is in a ROOT conflict's
% closing row. The break is measured: the pre-fix binary is rejected at `conclusion`.
var 1..5: x0 :: output_var;
var 1..5: x1 :: output_var;
var 1..5: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..5: x3 :: output_var;
var 1..5: x4 :: output_var;
var 1..5: x5 :: output_var;
var 1..5: x6 :: output_var;
constraint array_int_element(x1,[2,3,5,1,3],x0);
constraint array_int_element(x4,[2,5,2,1,4],x6);
constraint array_int_element(x6,[1,2,2,2,5],x4);
constraint int_ne(x4,x0);
constraint int_ne(x6,x3);
constraint int_ne(x6,x2);
constraint int_ne(x2,x4);
constraint int_lin_le([-1,1,1],[x5,x6,x2],0);
solve :: int_search([x3,x0,x4,x6,x1,x5,x2], largest, indomain_max, complete) satisfy;
